{%- doc -%}
  Echoes "1" when the current cart qualifies for free shipping, "0" when
  it does not. Nothing else — it is meant to be captured:

    {%- capture ship_ok -%}{%- render 'cart-ship-qualified' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign ship_ok = ship_ok | strip -%}

  Shipping is free on everything except a named set of accessories, and
  even those ship free when they travel with something that qualifies, so
  a single qualifying line unlocks the whole order.

  Kept in one place so the progress bar, the total's shipping line and
  anything added later cannot disagree about who qualifies.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Handles are wrapped in commas on both sides so that "nike-studs" can
    never match inside "nike-studs-pro".
  endcomment
  assign excluded_handles = ''
  for item in settings.cart_ship_excluded_products
    assign excluded_handles = excluded_handles | append: ',' | append: item.handle | append: ','
  endfor

  assign excluded_tag = settings.cart_ship_excluded_tag | strip

  assign qualifying = 0
  for line in cart.items
    assign is_excluded = false

    assign needle = ',' | append: line.product.handle | append: ','
    if excluded_handles contains needle
      assign is_excluded = true
    endif

    if excluded_tag != blank and line.product.tags contains excluded_tag
      assign is_excluded = true
    endif

    unless is_excluded
      assign qualifying = qualifying | plus: 1
    endunless
  endfor

  if qualifying > 0
    echo '1'
  else
    echo '0'
  endif
-%}
